  "kind": "bit-matching-detail",
  "title": "MINVERSE runs Doolittle LU with x87 double-rounded sites, a 1e-12 pivot threshold, and +0.0 zero canonicalization",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20131 through 16.0.20527, MINVERSE performs in-place Doolittle LU with partial pivoting (returning #NUM! when max |pivot| < 1e-12 and #VALUE! for non-square, empty, text, or logical matrices), solves column-by-column using x87 PC64-to-PC53 double-rounding at every multiply, divide, and subtract site, and canonicalizes zero entries in the output array to +0.0.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across 120 pinned MINVERSE rows (Excel 16.0.20131 and 16.0.20228) and 64 dcj9k_r26_regression rows (Excel 16.0.20527.20150), matching 2,243/2,243 full-bank and 120/120 pinned MINVERSE rows.",
